WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.459 --> 00:00:08.950
Approximately 1.26 billion cells in your body
will die and be replaced with new cells, in

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:12.410
the time it takes to watch this video.

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:17.699
Your body also makes a brand new skeleton
every three months and a completely new layer

00:00:17.699 --> 00:00:20.310
of skin every month.

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:22.060
Your body is remarkable.

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:28.099
Here’s some of the most amazing things your
body does.

00:00:28.099 --> 00:00:30.319
1.

00:00:30.319 --> 00:00:40.510
There’s 7.2 billion people in the world
yet no two are the same, even identical twins

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:42.289
are surprisingly dissimilar.

00:00:42.289 --> 00:00:47.649
It’s common knowledge that we all have a
unique fingerprint but did you know that every

00:00:47.649 --> 00:00:51.280
human has a unique tongue print too.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:52.280
2.

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:57.600
Scientists estimate there are 37.2 trillion
cells in the average human body.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:03.850
But the numbers are still mind blowing if
we go a bit larger than just cells.

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:10.079
Every square inch of your skin contains 6
metres of blood vessels, 3.6 metres of nerve

00:01:10.079 --> 00:01:16.799
fibres, 1,300 nerve cells and 100 sweat glands.

00:01:16.799 --> 00:01:23.070
Also if unravelled, your circulatory system,
that’s your arteries, veins and capillaries,

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:25.869
would stretch around the earth four times.

00:01:25.869 --> 00:01:26.869
3.

00:01:26.869 --> 00:01:32.740
The adult human body consists of 206 bones,
and more than half of those are in the hands

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:33.990
and feet.

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:34.990
4.

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:39.909
The largest artery runs down the centre of
your body, it’s called your aorta and it

00:01:39.909 --> 00:01:43.799
diameter is almost as large as a garden hose.

00:01:43.799 --> 00:01:49.240
By contrast, the smallest blood vessels in
your body, capillaries, are so small that

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:54.950
it would take 10 of them side by side to equal
the thickness of a single strand of human

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:55.950
hair.

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:56.950
5.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:00.439
The human body has some rather disgusting
habits too.

00:02:00.439 --> 00:02:07.870
Your body will lose 100 strands of hair per
day and over 10 billion flakes of skin.

00:02:07.870 --> 00:02:13.580
And your body produces 1.5 litres of mucus
every day.

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:18.900
Also over the course of your lifetime, your
body will produce two swimming pools worth

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:20.070
of saliva.

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:21.070
6.

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:24.940
Your body has the potential to become superhuman.

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:29.940
In cases of extreme danger adrenaline rushes
through your body, which leads to an increased

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:36.150
level of oxygen flow to your muscles, giving
your super human strength, seemingly from

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:37.150
nowhere.

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:42.690
There have been several cases of people single
handily, lifting cars and other heavy objects

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:44.640
to free loved ones.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:45.640
7.

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:48.300
Your body can also predict the weather.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:53.680
When a storm is on its way the pressure in
the atmosphere drops, which in turn makes

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:57.060
the pressure on your joint fluids rise.

00:02:57.060 --> 00:03:02.350
So if your joints are aching, it’s your
bodies way of telling you there’s a storm

00:03:02.350 --> 00:03:03.350
coming.

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:04.350
8.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:10.640
Nerve impulses that travel to and from your
brain travel as fast as 170 miles miles per

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:11.640
hour.

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:12.640
9.

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:14.470
Your brain can remember 50,000 different scents.

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:21.310
And smelling something you’ve smelt before
can actually trigger you to recall memories.

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:22.310
10.

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:29.270
Your body is surprisingly resourceful, you
could remove your stomach, spleen, one kidney,

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:36.620
80% of your intestines and 70% of your liver
and still be able to survive.

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:37.620
11.

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:43.370
The skin is the body’s largest organ but
it also acts as a huge shield wall against

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:44.370
bacteria.

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:49.010
The skin constantly secretes antibacterial
substances.

00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:52.290
Most bacteria that lands on the skin dies
instantly.

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:53.290
12.

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:57.820
Whenever we learn something new or create
a new memory our brain add a new connection

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:02.170
between it’s neurons, these connections
are called synapses.

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:07.340
During the fist month of a human’s life
the number of synapses in your brain increases

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:12.360
dramatically, from 50 trillion, to 1 quadrillion.

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:13.360
13.

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:19.510
Arguably one of the most important structural
parts of your body is your big toe.

00:04:19.510 --> 00:04:24.800
This seemingly insignificant appendage is
a crucial component in maintaining our balance

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:28.780
and propelling us forward whilst walking and
running.

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:29.780
14.

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:35.610
The human eye can distinguish up to a million
different colours and take in more information

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:41.030
in a single gaze than the largest telescope
known to man.

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:47.520
Which by the way is on a mountain top in northern
Chile and it’s creatively named the European

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.590
Extremely Large Telescope.

00:04:49.590 --> 00:04:50.590
15.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:56.000
But surprisingly your body is a lot less human
than you may think.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:00.030
In fact your body is actually more bacteria
than human.

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:03.909
For every cell in your body there are at least
10 bacteria.

00:05:03.909 --> 00:05:09.949
That’s hundreds of trillions of bacteria,
they live in every nook and cranny of your

00:05:09.949 --> 00:05:10.949
body.

00:05:10.949 --> 00:05:15.610
But don’t worry, less than 1 percent of
the bacteria in your body can cause disease

00:05:15.610 --> 00:05:16.759
or illness.

00:05:16.759 --> 00:05:30.279
The majority are beneficial to your health.

